    "problem_statement": "### Cursor Initialization Issue\n\n#### Description\n\nIt seems there's an issue with the initialization of the `Cursor` class in the `tweepy/cursor.py` file. The recent changes have caused the `Cursor` to not behave as expected, particularly when iterating over items or pages. This is affecting the ability to retrieve user timelines and friend/follower IDs correctly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\nHere's a simple way to reproduce the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom tweepy import Cursor, API\n\n# Assuming `api` is an authenticated API object\ncursor = Cursor(api.user_timeline, screen_name='Twitter').items(5)\ntry:\n    status = next(cursor)\n    print(status.user.screen_name)\nexcept AttributeError as e:\n    print(\"Error encountered:\", e)\n```\n\n#### Expected Results\n\nThe code should print the screen name of the user 'Twitter' for the first status retrieved.\n\n#### Actual Results\n\nAn `AttributeError` is raised, indicating that the cursor is not correctly initialized or iterated.\n\n#### Additional Information\n\nThis issue seems to be affecting multiple cursor-related functionalities, including `items()` and `pages()` methods. It would be great to have a look into the recent changes in the `BaseIterator` class to ensure the correct assignment of method, args, and kwargs."
